          "text": "Clinical Indication:\nGeneralized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at age 9, occurring approximately 3 times per month. Genetic etiology associated with a pathogenic PCDH19 c.918G>A variant. Seizures are drug responsive. Current antiseizure medication: zonisamide.\n\nTechnique:\nRoutine scalp EEG recording.\n\nFindings:\nNo electrographic findings were provided for interpretation. The presence or absence of interictal epileptiform discharges or electrographic seizures therefore cannot be assessed.\n\nImpression:\nLimited routine EEG report because electrographic data and findings were not provided. The clinical history is not sufficient to determine EEG abnormalities or ictal localization.",
